assistant: Subject: follow next_cursor to fetch all search result pages

Root cause: since vendor API 2026-10-01, `/products` returns results in pages and sets `next_cursor` (here 5 of 7 cable items, `next_cursor: "5"`). `search_products` only read the first page, so it returned fewer items than `total`. The fix in `src/tools/search_products.ts` keeps requesting `&cursor=<next_cursor>` (the `cursor` query parameter in the spec) and adds each page's items until there is no cursor left. v1 responses have no `next_cursor`, so they still make one request and give the same output. Typecheck, lint and the other 13 tests pass. The repro test still fails, but only with UNMATCHED_REQUEST: the recording has no `GET /products?q=cable&cursor=5`, and the test says to fix that by re-recording with `fiks rerecord`. I'm only allowed to run pnpm commands, so I couldn't re-record it, and the fix hasn't been checked against real second-page data yet. Separately, the new version also seems to send prices in cents (6900 for a cable), which still breaks `items.price.range`. The repro marks that as out of scope, so I left it alone.

